   988	/**Function*************************************************************
   989	
   990	  Synopsis    [Returns 1 if an stmap area-sensitive mode should reject a cut.]
   991	
   992	  Description [The area-sensitive guards are evaluated after matching the
   993	  candidate cut because their hypotheses need the candidate's actual mapper
   994	  area. In stmap6 exact-area recovery, a wide high-fanout cut is rejected only
   995	  when the existing match has slack and the candidate does not save at least
   996	  half an inverter area. In stmap7, the area-saving override additionally
   997	  requires more than two inverter delays of slack and excludes the highest
   998	  fanout-risk bucket. In stmap8, the override is further rejected when the
   999	  candidate match worsens mapper arrival by more than one quarter of an
  1000	  inverter delay. In stmap9, middle-slack candidates can recover area only
  1001	  when they are outside the highest fanout bucket, do not worsen mapper
  1002	  arrival, and save at least one inverter area. In stmap10, that middle-slack
  1003	  relief also requires the mapper node to be no deeper than level 96. In
  1004	  stmap11, that depth window is tightened to level 64. In stmap12, the same
  1005	  tight-depth relief is allowed only in the lower moderate fanout bucket. In
  1006	  stmap13, the same decision path also records exact-area guard statistics. In
  1007	  stmap14, the lower-moderate middle-slack relief must save two inverter areas
  1008	  instead of one. In stmap15, one-inverter relief is restored only after the
  1009	  mapper observes a high lower-moderate/middle-slack profile. In stmap16, the
  1010	  same behavior also reports each admitted relief choice. In stmap17, the
  1011	  adaptive one-inverter relief threshold also requires a material mapper-arrival
  1012	  improvement; arrival-neutral choices keep the stricter two-inverter fallback.
  1013	  In stmap18, the same decisions are preserved while near-miss rejected
  1014	  middle-slack candidates are logged. In stmap19, pre-profile one-inverter
  1015	  relief is seeded only by candidates with the same material arrival gain. In
  1016	  stmap20, the pre-profile seed is further limited to shallow nodes. In
  1017	  stmap21, deeper pre-profile seeds are allowed only with a much larger mapper
  1018	  arrival gain. In stmap22, the same deep-seed path is relaxed to a moderate
  1019	  mapper-arrival gain. In stmap23, moderate deep seeds also need near-critical
  1020	  existing mapper slack. In stmap24, the moderate deep slack gate is tightened
  1021	  to the lower edge of the critical slack window. In stmap25, the stmap24 rule
  1022	  is kept, and one moderate deep seed from the next slack band is admitted for
  1023	  ablation. In stmap26, the first such moderate seed is skipped and only the
  1024	  second qualifying seed is admitted. In stmap27, moderate deep candidates in
  1025	  the next slack band are admitted unless they match the high-reference,
  1026	  low-slack, stronger-moderate signature isolated by stmap26. In stmap28, that
  1027	  hard blocker is replaced by a soft area-margin penalty on high-reference
  1028	  moderate seeds whose slack and arrival-gain ratios resemble load-risky
  1029	  choices. In stmap29, the high-reference penalty is made continuous over the
  1030	  same seed band. In stmap30, the same load-risk surface is extended to
  1031	  high-reference strong deep seeds with a smaller continuous penalty. In
  1032	  stmap31, the strong-seed gain slope is damped to probe the penalty threshold.
  1033	  In stmap32, a cut-leaf load proxy adds a candidate-cut fanout-shape term to
